{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-03T09:00:56.579Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Source (`src/cli/`)**\n- `doctor.ts`: `DoctorCommandOptions` extends `CommandInputs` (only `report` remains), resolves inputs via `resolveInputs`, writes each check with its trailing `\\n`, and feeds a passed `config` into `runDoctorChecks` through its `loadConfig` dependency.\n- `serve.ts`: `ServeCommandOptions` extends `CommandInputs` (other options unchanged), resolves inputs, loads config at the same point, and writes the URL and export lines with their trailing `\\n`.\n\n**Tests**\n- Updated `tests/doctor-command-error.test.ts`, `tests/serve.test.ts`, `tests/serve-export.test.ts` for the trailing newline.\n- Added `tests/command-inputs-doctor-serve.test.ts` comparing `runCliCaptured` and direct calls for `osq doctor` and `osq serve --export`, plus a case proving a passed `config` reaches doctor's config check.\n\n**Bug found/fixed in-scope**\n- The CLI `--export <dir>` was broken: commander yields `options.export` while `index.ts` passed `exportDir`. Since `index.ts` is out of scope, `serveCommand` now accepts the commander key as a fallback, so `osq serve --export` actually exports. Documented in the result file.\n\n`pnpm verify` (typechecks, build, full test suite, lint) passes, as does the task verify. Result written to `openspec/changes/142-command-inputs/.run/results/4.md`."}}
